\title{predpower: Design-Stage Assessment of Out-of-Sample Prediction Accuracy}
\description{
Power-analysis-style calculations for prediction studies. Given a sample size, a number of predictors, an assumed in-sample signal and a design efficiency factor, returns the expected out-of-sample R-squared and the expected correlation between observed and predicted outcomes, under ordinary least squares and under ridge regression at the design-implied penalty. Computes the design efficiency factor from a covariate matrix, supplies confidence intervals for the assumed signal by inverting the noncentral F or, when there are more predictors than observations, by restricted maximum likelihood under the ridge prior, and solves for the sample size, signal, number of predictors or design efficiency a study would need to beat the sample mean. All quantities are computable before any outcome is observed.
